Your friend: Have you seen the new menu in the school canteen? They have changed everything this month.
You: Yes, I saw it yesterday. {{1}}
Your friend: There are more salads and fruit now, and the chips have gone.
You: Really? And {{2}}?
Your friend: Not really. The pasta is the same as before, but the portions are smaller.
You: I see. {{3}}
Your friend: I used to buy a sandwich, but now I bring a lunch box from home.
You: That sounds like a good idea. {{4}}
Your friend: Usually some rice, chicken and an apple. My mother prepares it the night before.
You: Nice! And {{5}}?
Your friend: About two euros a day. It’s much cheaper than the canteen.
Your friend: Why don’t you try it next week?
You: {{6}}
